    "entry": 0,
    "role": "user",
    "text": "OK. I'm using Repl.it and building in HTML, CSS and JS. Can you write me the code for a web app in Repl.it called Outreach Butler. It is a tool for sourcers and recruiters to help them write better outreach messages, from start to finish, near instantaneously. The app needs to have four input text boxes, named “What’s the Job Title?”, “Company Name?”, “Link the Job Description here:”, and “Tone” (e.g. friendly, professional, casual, etc). Under that will be a checkbox named “Use Emojis?”. Under that should be a Submit button.\nNow add a large open output text field under the submit button, that will generate the following text, filling in the placeholders with the user's input, when the user clicks the submit button:\n\nWrite me an outreach email with subject line, followed by 4 step follow up emails, to a passive candidate. I work for a company called <Company Name>, we're hiring <What’s the Job Title?> for our new projects, use a <Tone> tone, create a new subject line for each follow up email, include a small segment in the first email about the company and job using information from this website <Link the Job Description here:>.\n\nAlso add the sentence “ Use relevant emojis.” to the end to the output text if the user checks the box for <Use Emojis?>\nI want the design to be like Airbnb in both style and color scheme.\n\nAlso, before you list all of the code, give me a file by file guide to creating this web app.\n"
  }
]
